{"availability":"available","full":"samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench","name":"agent-cost-bench","description":"Reproducible denial-of-wallet (DoW) benchmark for tool-using LLM agents, scored on provider-billed tokens/USD.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T21:08:03Z","updated":"2026-10-02T20:18:41Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["ai-safety","anthropic","benchmark","denial-of-wallet","gemini","llm-agents","llm-security","prompt-injection","python","red-teaming"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Could an attacker make your LLM agent run up its own bill? Scan your tools and find out — offline, no API key.","dowbench scan reads your tool definitions and flags the ones whose shape matches the cost-amplification patterns this project measured against real models — an unbounded tool result, a pagination loop with no cap, a field that relays prior output back in. It makes no provider call, needs no key, and spends nothing: it reads schemas only, so a finding is a pattern match, not a prediction of your bill. You get a specific answer in seconds — which tool could blow up your cost, why, and the fix.","Behind the scan is a reproducible denial-of-wallet (DoW) benchmark: an attack × defense × model matrix scored on provider-billed tokens and USD (not an LLM judge), which is where the patterns — and the one real finding the scan is built on (an 8.8× amplification that only a result cap stopped) — come from. The scan is the front door; the benchmark is the evidence."],"features":["Cost as the outcome. Success means the attack made the episode cost at least N×","Defenses on the same yardstick. Every defense is scored against the undefended","Replayable results. Every call's raw usage and sanitized request body are kept, so"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"354cc419410f3f294c72fc873b5b92d158edd819fdf109de379063be0183bc50","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Could an attacker make your LLM agent run up its own bill? Scan your tools and find out — offline, no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"A defense that blocks everything must not count as a win, so dowbench charges each one for its cost on benign tasks (benign overhead = median benign cost under the defense ÷ the no-defense baseline, − 1; ADR 0001). resultcap neutralizes the attack while adding just +1.1% on benign tasks and completing 100 % of them; the other four sit within ±1.1% too — noise at n = 5.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"354cc419410f3f294c72fc873b5b92d158edd819fdf109de379063be0183bc50","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T20:18:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samuelrojas-dev/agent-cost-bench/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","hash":"354cc419410f3f294c72fc873b5b92d158edd819fdf109de379063be0183bc50","originalBytes":22966,"storedBytes":22966,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["run","dowbench","adr","tool","result","scan","cost","one","call","every","replay","attack","each","docs","model","benign","cap","results","agent","defense","provider","real","byte","defens